---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import MarketingChrome from "../../components/MarketingChrome.astro";

const phoneDisplay = "(501) 413-3386";
const tel = "tel:+15014133386";
const sms = "sms:+15014133386";
---

<Base
  title="Las Vegas Landscaper Websites, Free Demo First | NV Labs"
  description="A free demo website for your Las Vegas landscaping business with a quote form, photo gallery, and service area. Call or text (501) 413-3386."
  image="/og.png"
  robots="index, follow"
>
  <MarketingChrome>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Las Vegas landscapers</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Websites for Las Vegas landscapers who'd rather be outside</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Free demo first. Before and after gallery, quote form, and clear service area. Call or text
        to get started.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call {phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text me</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="photos-title">
      <h2 id="photos-title">Your work is the best sales pitch</h2>
      <p>
        A yard that went from dead grass to clean rock and desert plants says more than anything I
        could write. So I build your site around your photos.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'll set up a before and after gallery, sorted by job type if you want. Turf installs in one
        section, rock and gravel in another, irrigation fixes in another. Homeowners can scroll and
        picture their own yard.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="jobs-title">
      <h2 id="jobs-title">List the jobs you actually take</h2>
      <p>
        Desert yards need different work than yards back east. I'll write your services in plain
        words so people know if you're the right call:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Desert landscaping and xeriscape design</li>
        <li>Artificial turf installs and grass removal</li>
        <li>Drip irrigation installs and repairs</li>
        <li>Sprinkler and timer fixes</li>
        <li>Tree and palm trimming</li>
        <li>Rock, gravel, and decomposed granite</li>
        <li>Cleanups and regular maintenance</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you don't do something, we leave it off. That saves you from calls you'll just have to
        turn down.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="quote-title">
      <h2 id="quote-title">A quote form that gets you real details</h2>
      <p>
        "How much to redo my backyard?" is impossible to answer over text. Your quote form will ask
        the useful stuff up front: address or neighborhood, front or back yard, rough size, what they
        want done, and a spot to upload photos. You get a clear picture before you ever call them
        back.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="water-title">
      <h2 id="water-title">Water Smart and HOA questions</h2>
      <p>
        A lot of homeowners here are swapping grass for desert plants, and many of them ask about
        the Southern Nevada Water Authority's Water Smart Landscapes program. I'll add a short,
        careful section that points people to SNWA's official page for current rules. I won't list
        amounts or promise anyone qualifies, since those details change and it's their call to
        check. Many programs want approval before any grass comes out, so the site can remind them
        to check first.
      </p>
      <p>
        HOAs come up a lot too. A simple line like "We're happy to work with your HOA's design
        rules" answers a question before it gets asked.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="area-title">
      <h2 id="area-title">Your service area across the Valley</h2>
      <p>
        I'm based in Las Vegas, so I know how big this valley is. Your site will say exactly where
        you work, like Summerlin, Centennial Hills, Spring Valley, Enterprise, Henderson, or North
        Las Vegas. If you skip certain areas, we can say that too, so nobody's disappointed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
      <h2 id="demo-title">Built first, decided later</h2>
      <p>
        I build a free demo of your site and text you the link. Look at it between jobs. If you like
        it, I put it live. If not, no hard feelings and nothing owed. We work by call and text.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <div>
          <h3>Can customers send me photos of their yard through the site?</h3>
          <p>
            Yes. I can add a photo upload to your quote form, so you see the yard before you call
            back.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Will the site talk about turf rebates?</h3>
          <p>
            It can mention the Water Smart Landscapes program and link to SNWA for current details. I
            keep it general and don't state amounts, because the program sets its own rules.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>I don't have many before and after photos. Is that okay?</h3>
          <p>
            Sure. We can start with a few and add more as you finish jobs. Just text me new photos
            when you have them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
      <h2 id="cta-title">Let's get your landscaping demo started</h2>
      <p>Text me your business name and the kind of work you do.</p>
      <a class="phone-big" href={tel}>{phoneDisplay}</a>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href={tel}>Call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={sms}>Text</a>
      </div>
      <a class="back-home" href="/">Back to NV Labs home</a>
    </section>
  </MarketingChrome>
</Base>
